      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "COGNAC COWBOY (10) has gone under by very narrow margins as runner-up in both outings off a spell, the latest when he chased along the sprint lane to miss by a nose at Melton. Draws out on the second line so may need luck at some point but he is race fit now and is good enough to take out a race like this. LIGHTNING ORO (5) is a daughter of The Storm Inside on debut. Showed some ability when runner-up in a trial. Could score at her first appearance. BETTORS IDEAL (8) is a three-year-old colt from the Lawlor stable on debut. May need luck at some stage extracting from the inside of the second row but has shown some talent at the trials. SIR KITT (3) could be close to a win after placing in his last two trials, both from wider draws than this.",
